# Denylist for verify_public.sh.
#
# Copy to `.public-guard.conf` (git-ignored) and replace the placeholders with
# the real private paths and project names of the machine you work on. The
# entries are grep -E alternations, so `|` separates them and regex
# metacharacters must be escaped.
#
# Keeping the real list out of the repository is the point: a denylist that
# names the private directories defeats itself once it is published.
#
# verify_public.sh refuses to run when `.public-guard.conf` is absent. That is
# deliberate -- a guard that passes because it was not configured is worse than
# no guard, since it reports "ok" either way.

# Absolute paths that must never appear in a published file.
FORBIDDEN='/home/YOUR_USER|/YOUR/SHARED/MOUNT|/YOUR/DATA/MOUNT|YOUR_PRIVATE_RECORD_DIR'

# Private project / repository names that must never appear in a published file.
PROJECTS='your-private-project-a|your-private-project-b'
